            <ArticleTitle>Multifocal contact dermatitis to nitroderm TTS 5 with extensive postinflammatory hypermelanosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>249-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allergic contact dermatitis to nitroglycerin has been previously reported. A localized cutaneous burn-like reaction due to the transdermal device was recently described. We are presenting a case of recurrent allergic contact dermatitis due to nitroglycerin as well as to its delivery device, resulting in numerous patches of postinflammatory hypermelanosis at the sites of application.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
